From db31a332630f19dd811196b13bbb3a99d0caedcb Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: callan <callanf@nvidia.com>
Date: Thu, 12 Nov 2026 18:45:33 +1000
Subject: [PATCH 11/38] feat(replay): fan-out replicas on path B
 (kv.replicate), unused unless a policy sends it

KvAction::Replicate { source_scheduler_id, block_hashes, local_hashes } on a target rank:
KvBlockCommand::Replicate stages one KVCR pull from the source into the target's G2 of the leading
blocks of the chain the target lacks, detached from any request (it lands as any pull does).
Done, Partial or Failed by the blocks staged; Unsupported without KVCR or toward itself. Test: a
replica pulls a peer prefix into G2 without a request; nothing more once held, nothing from itself
or without KVCR.
